== 2. THE FIX — THE EXISTING GATE, NOT A SECOND ONE ==
tests/test_served.py has carried the export gate since W12 (MC 11274.1.21): it skips on
`not os.path.isfile(static/index.html)` with a reason naming tools/export_web.sh. This
card reuses THAT condition and THAT reason sentence on the one leg that needs them — the
only new constants are `INDEX` (the same path) and `NO_EXPORT` (test_served.py's sentence
verbatim, minus only its trailing "(W12 DoD runs it present)" parenthetical, which names
another card's run). Importing the constant instead of restating it was PROBED and
REJECTED (import-probe-skip-propagates.log, a minimal /tmp pair mirroring the two module
shapes): the module-level Skipped propagates through the import and the importer collects
NO test of its own, so sharing by import would skip all 8 scaffold legs. The gate lands
as a per-test
`@pytest.mark.skipif` rather than a module-level skip because a module skip would take
this file's OTHER seven legs with it: they read
committed files only and must keep running with no export — and
test_server_path_escape_is_404_json_not_found is the one leg that is STRONGER without an
export (its 404 then comes from a missing file, not from the extension allowlist).
Alternatives weighed and NOT built, so nobody re-adds them: a GW_EXPORT env var; a
conftest helper/fixture; a second skip-list; deleting the leg (the served 200/html/title
contract is real, it just needs the artifact).

